The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused:
1. `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there's no index 1

I fixed it by changing `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and all tests now pass successfully.
